SETTINGS + AUTH/ROLES/PERMISSIONS — PHASED IMPLEMENTATION TRACKER
====================================================
Read this file top to bottom before doing anything. If resuming a fresh
session: find the first phase NOT marked [DONE], read its own checklist for
partial progress, and continue from there. Say "bu todo dosyasında [Faz N]
fazından devam et" to resume a specific phase.

====================================================
PHASE 0 — Settings module (mock-store, no auth yet)  [DONE]
====================================================
Full Settings area: 13 sections, canonical InstitutionSettings model,
permission-ready metadata (not enforced yet), Kurum Bilgileri, Eğitim
Türleri, Seans/Takvim/Finans/Hakediş/Öğrenci/Bildirim/Kullanıcılar/Veri/
Görünüm/Güvenlik/İşlem Geçmişi sections, settings overview page.
Completed across two sessions (initial build + finishing security/audit
pages + a dashboard responsive-layout bugfix unrelated to settings).

====================================================
PHASE 1 — Auth/Roles/Permissions Foundation  [DONE]
====================================================
- AuthService interface + LocalAuthService (Web Crypto SHA-256 hashing,
  mock-only, documented as such).
- Canonical Role/Permission model replacing the old UserRole/AppUserRole
  split — src/types/auth.ts, src/lib/auth/{roles,permission-catalog,
  permissions,route-permissions}.ts.
- AuthProvider/useAuth() — session timeout, inactivity logout+warning
  banner, activity tracking.
- Real /login (Turkish errors, lockout messaging, ?next= redirect).
- RouteGuard on every /app/* route (unauth -> /login, unauthorized ->
  /app/403). Sidebar/nav filtered per-item by permissionKey.
- Full-store localStorage persistence (versioned, src/lib/mock/
  persistence.ts) — not debounced (a debounced write raced fast reload/
  relogin and lost the session; fixed).
- 7 seeded demo accounts (all password Demo1234!) — see Phase 3, three of
  these roles are REMOVED there, read Phase 3 before relying on this list:
  owner/admin/teacher/accounting/front_desk/viewer/guardian.
- Audit expansion: login_success/failed, account_locked, logout,
  password_changed, user_updated/deactivated/activated, role_changed.
- Migrated SettingsAccessGuard, SettingsShell, FinancePage guard,
  settings/data, settings/users to the new permission system. Deleted the
  old src/lib/permissions.ts.
- Verified: tsc clean, eslint clean, 14 Playwright QA scenarios passed
  (unauth redirect, per-role login+nav, lockout, logout, reload
  persistence, resetToDemo).
- Known pre-existing (not introduced by this work): store.tsx has ~13
  react-compiler "Cannot access refs during render" lint findings — this
  is the file's own pre-existing ref-caching convention (11 already
  existed before this work), left as-is for consistency rather than
  refactoring unrelated code.

====================================================
PHASE 2 — Roles UI / Invitations / Password Reset  [DONE]
====================================================
- Settings → Kullanıcılar ve Roller rebuilt as 4 tabs: Kullanıcılar /
  Roller / Yetki Matrisi / Davetler (src/components/settings/users/*,
  src/app/(app)/app/settings/users/page.tsx).
- Role store mutators: createRole/updateRole/deactivateRole (usage-
  protected, system roles never deactivatable). Role.key loosened from
  the RoleKey union to `string` so custom roles work.
- Roller tab: create/clone/edit roles, permission editor grouped by
  module (src/components/settings/users/RolePermissionEditor.tsx), new
  src/components/ui/{tabs,checkbox}.tsx primitives.
- Yetki Matrisi tab: roles x permissions grid, click-to-toggle.
- Invitations: real single-use 7-day tokens (src/types/auth.ts's
  Invitation), Davetler tab (copy link/resend/revoke),
  /accept-invite?token= page, LocalAuthService.acceptInvitation.
- Password reset: /forgot-password + /reset-password?token= wired to
  real (mock-delivery) token flow, LocalAuthService.requestPasswordReset/
  resetPassword now implemented (were Phase-1 stubs). Login page's
  "Şifremi unuttum" re-enabled.
- Kullanıcılar tab polish: search/filter by role+status, lock/unlock
  ("Etkinleştir" also clears lockout fields), resend invitation,
  teacher/guardian record linking in the invite/edit form.
- Verified: tsc clean, eslint clean, 11 Playwright QA scenarios passed.
  One test-methodology gotcha worth remembering: Playwright's
  `browser.newPage()` creates an ISOLATED context per call (does not
  share localStorage) — use one `browser.newContext()` + `context.
  newPage()` per scenario that needs shared storage, or tests will show
  false failures that look like auth/persistence bugs.

====================================================
PHASE 3 — Role simplification / Resource scoping / Role dashboards /
          Remaining settings activation   [DONE]
====================================================
- Removed Muhasebe/Danışma/Görüntüleyici from SYSTEM_ROLES (src/lib/auth/
  roles.ts) and their seeded demo accounts. 4 system roles remain: Sahip,
  Yönetici, Öğretmen, Veli. RoleKey union narrowed to match; Role.key is
  still `string` so custom-role creation (Phase 2) is untouched.
- migrateRemovedRoleId() in roles.ts + a one-time mount effect in
  store.tsx migrate any persisted AppUser still pointing at a removed
  roleId to role-admin (Yönetici) and log a `role_changed` audit entry —
  verified against an injected stale localStorage snapshot, not just the
  clean seed data.
- src/lib/auth/scope.ts (+ use-scope.ts hook): CurrentUserScope keyed off
  AuthUser.teacherId/guardianId (not role name), getScopedStudents/
  Sessions/Teachers/Guardians/Payments/Installments, canAccessStudent/
  Teacher/Guardian/Session. Applied to: students list+detail, sessions
  list, calendar (+ mobileDefaultView/showWeekends settings wired in same
  pass), teacher detail, guardian detail, payments+installments list.
  Detail pages use an UnauthorizedState guard; list pages just render
  scoped data — direct-URL access to another teacher's/guardian's/
  student's record is additionally blocked by RouteGuard itself (neither
  role has teachers.view/guardians.view), confirmed via QA.
- Guardian role gained students.view + finance.student_payments.view
  (Phase 1 had granted neither, blocking guardian from reaching either
  page at all); calendar.view deliberately NOT granted (spec's guardian
  nav omits Takvim — the scoped Guardian Dashboard's own upcoming-
  sessions list covers "when is my child's next session" instead).
- Role-specific dashboards: OwnerDashboard (existing content, unchanged,
  now one branch of dashboard/page.tsx) vs new TeacherDashboard.tsx
  (own today/week sessions, own students, earnings card only if
  teachers.view_earnings granted, reuses TodaysScheduleCard/
  UpcomingSessionsCard/RecentSessionsTable with scoped data — no new
  components needed for those) vs new GuardianDashboard.tsx (child
  switcher when >1 linked student, billed/paid/balance summary, scoped
  upcoming+recent sessions). dashboard/page.tsx branches on
  useUserScope() before rendering any of the three.
- Nav filtering was already permission-driven (Phase 1) — no code change
  needed beyond the guardian permission grants above; verified the
  resulting nav for teacher (Panel/Takvim/Öğrenciler/Seanslar only) and
  guardian (Panel/Öğrenciler/Seanslar/Öğrenci Ödemeleri only) matches the
  spec's lists exactly.
- Settings activated this phase (targeted subset, not exhaustive — see
  "remaining" below): sessions.timeStepMinutes (session form's time
  input step), calendar.mobileDefaultView + calendar.showWeekends,
  appearance.sidebarDefaultState (first-visit-only, user's own toggle
  always wins after), appearance.defaultLandingPage (root page + post-
  login redirect, both via new src/lib/settings/landing-page.ts),
  finance.highlightOverdueInstallments (red row highlight on the
  Payments page's installment table).
- NOT activated this phase (still saved-but-unused — see the audit that
  informed this list): sessions.cancellationMinNoticeHours/
  makeupSessionBehavior; calendar.workingDays/weekStartsOn/colorSource/
  timeFormat; finance.allowInstallments/defaultInstallmentIntervalDays/
  overpaymentPolicy/receiptNumberFormat; ALL of teacherEarnings.* (no
  consumer wired at all yet); students.autoGenerateStudentNumber/
  studentNumberFormat (Student type has no studentNumber field — this is
  a data-model change, not just a wiring change, deliberately not rushed
  late in this phase); students.guardianRequired/requireBirthDate/
  requireKvkkConsent/requireHealthInfo/requireEmergencyContact (no form-
  validation consumer yet); appearance.density/tableRowDensity/
  cardRadius (would need CSS-variable threading across the whole UI, out
  of scope for a targeted pass); documents.* (dateFormat/csvDelimiter/
  pdfPageSize/defaultExportOrientation/receiptTitle — no export/format
  consumer wired). None of these are backend/provider-only — they're
  legitimate remaining wiring work for a future phase.
- Verified: tsc clean, eslint clean on every touched/created file
  (store.tsx's pre-existing react-compiler "refs" findings unchanged in
  count beyond the 2 already accepted in Phase 1/2 — see that phase's
  note). 20/20 Playwright QA scenarios passed: removed-account login
  rejected, teacher dashboard+nav+scoped list+blocked-from-other-teacher,
  guardian dashboard+nav+scoped list+blocked-from-other-
  guardian+blocked-from-unrelated-student, reload persistence for a
  scoped role, and the removed-role migration test against an injected
  stale snapshot. Separately re-ran the full owner/admin flow (dashboard,
  students, teachers, guardians, sessions, calendar, payments, settings/
  users, finance) — zero console errors, zero regressions from the new
  branching.

====================================================
DEFERRED — not yet scheduled to a phase
====================================================
- Remaining settings activation (see Phase 3's "NOT activated" list for
  the exact field-by-field breakdown): session cancellation-notice/
  makeup-billing rules, calendar working-days/week-start/color-source/
  time-format, finance installment-availability/overpayment-policy/
  receipt-numbering, ALL of teacherEarnings.* (currently zero consumers),
  student-number auto-generation (needs a Student.studentNumber field —
  a data-model change, not just wiring), student/guardian required-field
  validation rules, appearance density/card-radius (CSS-variable
  threading across the whole UI), documents.* (date/CSV/PDF export
  formatting).
- Notification engine (email/SMS/WhatsApp — provider-ready adapters only,
  in-app notifications already exist and work).
- Dedicated "Bildirimler" nav page for the guardian nav list — today
  guardians are pointed at the topbar bell instead (see GuardianDashboard's
  own note); the spec's guardian nav item exists but has no dedicated
  route.
- Teacher's "own earnings if permitted" as a dedicated nav item/page —
  today it's a stat card on the Teacher Dashboard only; the institution-
  wide "Öğretmen Hakedişleri" page/route was deliberately NOT reused or
  scoped for this (it shows every teacher's earnings, would need its own
  scoping pass first).
- SupabaseAuthService / server-side+DB-level authorization / RLS / tenant
  isolation — this whole project is intentionally mock/local-store only
  so far; production migration is a reporting deliverable (checklist),
  never implemented against a real backend in any phase so far.
- ActionGuard/SensitiveActionGuard components (confirm-before-mutating
  wrappers) — mentioned in the original spec's centralized-helpers list,
  never built; today's dangerous actions (data reset, role deactivation)
  use ad-hoc typed-confirmation dialogs instead, which work but aren't
  the generic component the spec envisioned.
- Full Profile page editing beyond read-only info + change-password
  (avatar, notification preferences, default landing page, active-
  sessions/device placeholder).

